[1.001,"o","\u001b[17A\r\u001b[48;2;43;48;59m \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;192;197;206;48;2;43;48;59mWait /\"replicas\": 5/\u001b[0m\u001b[48;2;43;48;59m                                                       \u001b[0m\u001b[1B\r\u001b[48;2;43;48;59m \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;192;197;206;48;2;43;48;59mScreenshot after\u001b[0m\u001b[48;2;43;48;59m                                                           \u001b[0m\u001b[1B\r\u001b[48;2;43;48;59m \u001b[0m\u001b[38;2;192;197;206;48;2;43;48;59mCtrl+C\u001b[0m\u001b[48;2;43;48;59m                                                                     \u001b[0m\u001b[1B\r\u001b[48;2;43;48;59m                                                                            \u001b[0m\u001b[1B\r\u001b[K\u001b[1B\rThe recorder runs it in \u001b[1;36;40mbash\u001b[0m on a real PTY with a pinned environment,       \u001b[1B\rfollows the screen with a\r\u001b[26CVT emulator,\r\u001b[39Cand writes:\u001b[2B\r\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mper \u001b[1;36;40mScreenshot\u001b[0m: a PNG in a window frame, an SVG with selectable text, and\u001b[1B\r\u001b[1m   \u001b[0ma text grid;                                                             \u001b[1B\r\u001b[1m • \u001b[0man asciinema v2 cast, with input events and the palette in its header;   \u001b[1B\r\u001b[1m • \u001b[0ma GIF with a key overlay, and an MP4 when FFmpeg is installed.           \u001b[1B\r\u001b[K\u001b[1B\r\u001b[1;36;40mcheck\u001b[0m compares a new run's text grids with committed ones, so documentation \u001b[1B\rmedia cannot drift from the program it shows.                               \u001b[1B\r\u001b[K\u001b[1B\r\u001b[1C\u001b[48;2;43;48;59m                                   \u001b[0m\u001b[1B\r\u001b[7C\u001b[2m8–34 of 51 · ↑↓ PgUp PgDn · q quits\u001b[0m"]
